      "side": 1,
      "message": "Implemented as a runnable Bazel target so we have something concrete: change 620501 — bazel run //tools/bzl:gerrit-maven-mirror-check.\n\n@matthias.sohn@gmail.com — It reads the lock and HEAD-probes the mirror directly, so it\u0027s cache-independent, and bazel run has no result cache: a local run and a CI run of the same command can\u0027t diverge.\n\n@luca.milanesio@gmail.com — one command, identical locally and in CI, naming the missing coordinate, so no \"works for me.\" Run first, short-circuiting the build, it stops before any Central fetch — protecting the mirror/Central from the 429 case. Only a genuine 404 is a miss (exit 1); network/mirror errors are exit 2, so a blip doesn\u0027t false-block. Contributors can\u0027t upload, so the request path is documented in `dev-bazel.txt` and `dev-processes.txt` \"Upgrading Libraries\".\n\nNo new label or SR — it gates the existing Verified.\n\nIf the direction\u0027s right, next step is the CI wiring.",
